CM_ SG_ 2147548910 EngineIntercoolerTemperature "Engine Intercooler Temperature: Temperature of liquid found in the intercooler located after the turbocharger.";
CM_ SG_ 2147548910 EngnTrhrgr1OlTmprtr "Engine Turbocharger 1 Oil Temperature: Temperature of the turbocharger lubricant.";
CM_ SG_ 2147548910 EngineOilTemperature1 "Engine Oil Temperature 1: Temperature of the engine lubricant.Note:  If there is only one engine oil temperature measurement, this SP should be used.  This is the SP that is typically displayed on an on-highway truck instrument cluster.See also SPNs ...";
CM_ SG_ 2147548910 EngineFuel1Temperature1 "Engine Fuel 1 Temperature 1: Temperature of fuel (or gas) of the first fuel type. See SPN 3468 for a second temperature measurement of the first fuel type.";
CM_ SG_ 2147548910 EngineCoolantTemperature "Engine Coolant Temperature: Temperature of liquid found in engine cooling system.";
CM_ BO_ 2147548911 "Engine Fluid Level/Pressure 1";
CM_ SG_ 2147548911 EngineCoolantLevel1 "Engine Coolant Level 1: Ratio of volume of liquid found in engine cooling system to total cooling system volume.  Typical monitoring location is in the coolant expansion tank.";
CM_ SG_ 2147548911 EngineCoolantPressure1 "Engine Coolant Pressure 1: Gage pressure of liquid found in engine cooling system.See SPN 20 for alternate range and resolution.";
CM_ SG_ 2147548911 EngineCrankcasePressure1 "Engine Crankcase Pressure 1: First instance of the gage pressure inside engine crankcase.";
CM_ SG_ 2147548911 EngineOilPressure1 "Engine Oil Pressure 1: Gage pressure of oil in engine lubrication system as provided by oil pump.  See SPN 7468 for alternate resolution.";
CM_ SG_ 2147548911 EngineOilLevel "Engine Oil Level: Ratio of current volume of engine sump oil to maximum required volume.";
CM_ SG_ 2147548911 EngnExtnddCrnksBlwBPrssr "Engine Extended Crankcase Blow-by Pressure: Differential crankcase blow-by pressure as measured through a tube with a venturi. (SPN 1264 is not to be used â€“ obsolete)";
CM_ SG_ 2147548911 EngineFuelDeliveryPressure "Engine Fuel Delivery Pressure: Gage pressure of fuel in system as delivered from supply pump to the injection pump.  See SPN 7469 for alternate resolution.See also SPN 5578 for Fuel Delivery Absolute Pressure.";
CM_ BO_ 2147548913 "Cruise Control/Vehicle Speed 1";
CM_ SG_ 2147548913 EngineShutdownOverrideSwitch "Engine Shutdown Override Switch: Switch signal which indicates the position of the engine shutdown override switch.  This switch function allows the operator to override an impending engine shutdown.00b = Off01b = On10b = Error11b = Not available...";
CM_ SG_ 2147548913 EngineDiagnosticTestModeSwitch "Engine Diagnostic Test Mode Switch: Switch signal which indicates the position of the engine diagnostic test mode switch.00b = Off01b = On10b = Error11b = Not available";
CM_ SG_ 2147548913 EngineIdleDecrementSwitch "Engine Idle Decrement Switch: Switch signal which indicates the position of the idle decrement switch.00b = Off01b = On10b = Error11b = Not available";
CM_ SG_ 2147548913 EngineIdleIncrementSwitch "Engine Idle Increment Switch: Switch signal which indicates the position of the idle increment switch.00b = Off01b = On10b = Error11b = Not available";
CM_ SG_ 2147548913 CruiseControlStates "Cruise Control States: This parameter is used to indicate the current state, or mode, of operation by the cruise control device.  This is a status parameter.000b = Off/Disabled001b = Hold010b = Accelerate011b = Decelerate100b = Resume101b = Set110b =...";
CM_ SG_ 2147548913 PtoGovernorState "PTO Governor State: This parameter is used to indicate the current state or mode of operation by the power takeoff (PTO) governor.  In lieu of support for PTO Drive Engagement parameters, this parameter may represent the status of a PTO drive.  The b...";
CM_ SG_ 2147548913 CruiseControlSetSpeed "Cruise Control Set Speed: Value of set (chosen) velocity of velocity control system.  See SPN 6809 for an alternate resolution.If an algorithm that can modify the cruise control set point exists in the system, such as Predictive Cruise Control or Ada...";
CM_ SG_ 2147548913 CruiseControlAccelerateSwitch "Cruise Control Accelerate Switch: Switch signal of the cruise control activator which indicates that the activator is in the position accelerate.00b = Cruise control activator not in the position accelerate01b = Cruise control activator in position a...";
CM_ SG_ 2147548913 CruiseControlResumeSwitch "Cruise Control Resume Switch: Switch signal of the cruise control activator which indicates that the activator is in the position resume.00b = Cruise control activator not in the position resume01b = Cruise control activator in position resume10b = E...";
CM_ SG_ 2147548913 CrsCntrlCstDlrtSwth "Cruise Control Coast (Decelerate) Switch: Switch signal of the cruise control activator which indicates that the activator is in the position coast (decelerate).00b = Cruise control activator not in the position coast01b = Cruise control activator in...";
CM_ SG_ 2147548913 CruiseControlSetSwitch "Cruise Control Set Switch: Switch signal of the cruise control activator which indicates that the activator is in the position set.00b = Cruise control activator not in the position set01b = Cruise control activator in position set10b = Error11b = No...";
CM_ SG_ 2147548913 ClutchSwitch "Clutch Switch: Switch signal which indicates that the clutch pedal is being pressed. It is necessary for a safe drivetrain behavior that the clutch switch is set before the clutch is opened (cruise control function).00b = Clutch pedal released01b = C...";
CM_ SG_ 2147548913 BrakeSwitch "Brake Switch: Switch signal which indicates that the driver operated brake foot pedal is being pressed.  This brake foot pedal is controlling the vehicles' service brake (total vehicle braking application, not park brakes).  It is necessary for safe ...";
CM_ SG_ 2147548913 CruiseControlEnableSwitch "Cruise Control Enable Switch: Switch signal which indicates that it is possible to manage the cruise control function.00b = Cruise control disabled01b = Cruise control enabled10b = Error11b = Not available";
CM_ SG_ 2147548913 CruiseControlActive "Cruise Control Active: Cruise control is switched on.  It is not ensured that the engine is controlled by cruise control, as in the case of a large driver's demand the engine is controlled by the driver while cruise control is active (maximum selecti...";
CM_ SG_ 2147548913 WheelBasedVehicleSpeed "Wheel-Based Vehicle Speed: Speed of the vehicle as calculated from wheel or tailshaft speed.";
CM_ SG_ 2147548913 ParkBrakeReleaseInhibitRequest "Park Brake Release Inhibit Request: Park Brake Release Inhibit Request signals the desire that an applied park brake remain applied and limit the ability of the vehicle to be moved.  00b = Park Brake Release Inhibit not requested01b = Park Brake Rele...";
CM_ SG_ 2147548913 CruiseControlPauseSwitch "Cruise Control Pause Switch: Switch signal which indicates the position of the Cruise Control Pause Switch used on Remote Cruise Control applications. The Cruise Control Pause Switch signal temporarily disables the Cruise Control function.00b = Off01...";
CM_ SG_ 2147548913 ParkingBrakeSwitch "Parking Brake Switch: Switch signal which indicates when the parking brake is set. In general the switch actuated by the operator's park brake control, whether a pedal, lever or other control mechanism  (see also SPN 619 and 5275).00b = Parking brake...";
CM_ SG_ 2147548913 TwoSpeedAxleSwitch "Two Speed Axle Switch: Switch signal which indicates the current axle range.00b = Low speed range01b = High speed range10b = Error11b = Not available";
CM_ BO_ 2147548919 "Vehicle Electrical Power 1";
CM_ SG_ 2147548919 KeySwitchBatteryPotential "Key Switch Battery Potential: Battery potential measured at the input of the electronic control unit supplied through a key switch or similar switching device.Note:  See SPN 22624 for a discrete state indication of the Key Switch input.";
CM_ SG_ 2147548919 BatteryPotentialPowerInput1 "Battery Potential / Power Input 1: This parameter measures the first source of battery potential as measured at the input of the ECU/actuator etc. coming from one or more batteries, irrespective of the distance between the component and the battery. ...";
CM_ SG_ 2147548919 ChargingSystemPotentialVoltage "Charging System Potential (Voltage): Electrical potential measured at the charging system output.  The charging system may be any device charging the batteries.  This includes alternators, generators, solid state charger and other charging devices.";
CM_ SG_ 2147548919 AlternatorCurrent "Alternator Current: Measure of electrical current flow from the alternator.  Alternator Current (High Range/Resolution) parameter SPN 1795 has a higher range and resolution of the same parameter.";
CM_ SG_ 2147548919 SliBattery1NetCurrent "SLI Battery 1 Net Current: Net flow of electrical current into/out of the first battery or first set of batteries used for starting the engine, for lighting, and for ignition (SLI).  If more than one battery is included in the first set of batteries ...";
